        "original_id": "999f0ec6-aab2-5108-9e39-d27d8dcc63af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kerry Saxby-Junna, Cathy Freeman, Jana Pittman, Sally Pearson, Dimitri Markov, Jared Tallent, Mitchell Watt\n- Places: Young, New South Wales, Ballina, New South Wales\n- Topics: Australia at the World Championships in Athletics, 2011 census\n\nFacts:\n- Kerry Saxby-Junna was born in Young, New South Wales, and grew up in Ballina, New South Wales.\n- At the 2011 census, Young, New South Wales, had a population of 6,960.\n- Cathy Freeman, Jana Pittman, and Sally Pearson are Australia's only multiple gold medal winners at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Cathy Freeman also won a bronze medal, and Sally Pearson also won a silver medal, at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Other Australian multiple medalists at the World Championships in Athletics include Dimitri Markov with 1 gold and 1 silver, Jared Tallent with 1 silver and 2 bronzes, Kerry Saxby-Junna with 1 silver and 1 bronze, and Mitchell Watt with 1 silver and 1 bronze.",
